WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.163 --> 00:00:00.996
- What's your name by the way?

00:00:00.996 --> 00:00:01.829
- [Thoraya] Thoraya.

00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:02.710
- Terry.
- Nice to meet you, man.

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.520
- Pleasure.
- All right give me a second.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.408
- Naw, I'm playing (laughs)

00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:08.330
(Thoraya laughs)

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.470
- [Thoraya] All right,
man, what's your name?

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.303
- Terry.

00:00:10.303 --> 00:00:12.000
- [Thoraya] Okay, and what's your story?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.350
- Well I fell in love with a woman

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.660
and she ruined my life.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.923
Naw, I'm playing (laughs), I'm kidding.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.350
Well, my story on how I got to San Diego

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.823
or how I got here?

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.930
Well, I sold my mansion
for a penny, no (laughs).

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:31.512
Well,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:34.793
I've

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.900
had my ups and downs

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.205
but I won't blame anybody.

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:41.960
I

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.723
had,

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.720
I've been battling alcohol

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:52.823
for

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.970
some years now and

00:00:57.654 --> 00:00:59.520
I've had a house,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.410
I've had a couple houses
and a couple cars (laughs)

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.537
and couple wives, no I'm playing (laughs).

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.410
But alcohol eventually

00:01:11.405 --> 00:01:13.200
dragged me down.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.850
So I've had to start over

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.890
and I'm in the process
of starting over again.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.320
- [Thoraya] Can I ask
a follow-up question?

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.630
- Of course.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.320
- [Thoraya] So you said that alcohol is,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.543
well you would say,
the main reason, right?

00:01:27.543 --> 00:01:31.670
- Alcohol is the only
reason for everything.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.440
My dad's an alcoholic and
his father's an alcoholic,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.910
everyone in my family's an alcoholic,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.583
so I had to make sure I
carry the family tradition.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.210
It started off as

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.860
a casual

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.880
social

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.193
thing,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.130
like smoking an occasional cigarette

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.990
every now and then at a party

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.890
or whatever your reason is.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.390
And then it became its own

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:01.643
monster.

00:02:01.643 --> 00:02:02.476
I

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.270
not sure if there's another
adequate word for it

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.530
but it becomes,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.530
it becomes its own thing
eventually, eventually.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.830
What do you think people think?

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.600
- [Thoraya] I mean, when I,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.620
I've had friends in the car with me

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.960
and, like, I've seen a homeless
person and I've stopped

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.450
and I've given the homeless person money,

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.727
and they've told me, like,
"Why would you do that?

00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:30.450
"They're gonna spend it on this."

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.573
And I'm like, "You don't know that."

00:02:31.573 --> 00:02:32.980
- Can't make an assumption,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.470
you'd don't know what
they're gonna spend it on.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.610
- [Thoraya] Yeah, exactly.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.496
- You could ask them if
it bothers you that much.

00:02:38.496 --> 00:02:39.355
- [Thoraya] Right (laughs).

00:02:39.355 --> 00:02:40.796
- You know what I mean, right (laughs)?

00:02:40.796 --> 00:02:42.254
- [Thoraya] Yeah, there you go.

00:02:42.254 --> 00:02:43.330
- "What are you gonna
spend this money on?"

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.542
If they say crack, then
you snatch it back (laughs)

00:02:45.542 --> 00:02:47.900
(Thoraya laughs)

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.030
Hardest thing is having a
certain level of commitment,

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.350
a certain level of

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.910
status, and then losing that

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:58.800
and starting

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.420
all over again,

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.650
and then getting it back

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.667
and then starting all
over again (chuckles).

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.993
That sucks.

00:03:11.179 --> 00:03:13.457
- Well, you know, I started off with a,

00:03:13.457 --> 00:03:16.657
you know, a lot of people
like to think that it would be

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.880
that I had a bad childhood
or something like that.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.740
It wasn't like that.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.250
I mean, I loved my childhood,

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.850
I loved my mother, I loved my family.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.582
You know, I had a good upbringing,

00:03:28.582 --> 00:03:31.493
a great relationship, I was
very successful in business.

00:03:33.244 --> 00:03:34.560
I guess somewhere officially

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.543
I have about nine years of college.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.300
In one night, in just one night,

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.340
I lost my wife, I lost my daughter,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:48.110
I lost my house, I lost my car.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.950
I like to say that, "Oh, we
can get through anything."

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.600
You know what, if you can get
through what I just told you,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.600
you're not human (laughs).

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.580
Some things you just, you know,
you just can't get through.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.867
I don't care who you are,

00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:02.940
you know, a series of events
could knock anybody down.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.080
Life to me now is really
kind of such a blur.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.270
I mean, the only life I know

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.433
is the one that I have
right in front of me now.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.520
How do you go about going into recovery

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.210
and trying to be clean and sober

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:18.390
when there's no reason?

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.730
I'm not gonna give anything back.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.240
Who do I have to give?

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.010
There's nobody to give it to.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.203
Tried to kill myself.

00:04:27.052 --> 00:04:29.320
I had a full prescription of Xanax,

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.450
60 milligrams, a full
prescription of Trazodone.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.533
I woke up well rested, I
can't even kill myself.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.300
I guess there's some sort of a purpose

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.890
or something for me 'cause
I'm still here (chuckles).

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.000
There's gotta be, 'cause there's no way

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.280
I should've lived through that.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.380
There was a meeting I went to.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.057
In that meeting a guy
came up to me and he says,

00:04:50.057 --> 00:04:51.957
"I heard your story, I heard it.

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:53.227
"About three and a half years ago

00:04:53.227 --> 00:04:55.180
"I was at Pathfinders."

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.530
That was a recovery home I went to.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.977
And he says, "Well, I
heard your story there.

00:04:59.977 --> 00:05:01.687
"Then I heard it again,
it ran through my mind

00:05:01.687 --> 00:05:03.167
"while I stood on the Coronado Bridge

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.847
"right before I jumped,
and I didn't jump that day.

00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:08.214
"That was three and half years ago."

00:05:08.214 --> 00:05:09.677
He said, "I got six guys I sponsor

00:05:09.677 --> 00:05:11.817
"and all of 'em know your story.

00:05:11.817 --> 00:05:12.650
"Did you ever think for a moment

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.567
"that your life may be
not about yours anymore?

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.400
"Maybe it's not about you?"

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.200
If my story can save a few lives,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.010
that's enough purpose in itself,

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.130
and you know what, I
have found purpose since,

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.556
and that is it.

00:05:25.556 --> 00:05:28.220
You know, you gotta
understand that not everybody

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.433
is evil out here.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.620
And if you keep on turning your blind eye,

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.830
you're gonna turn your
blind eye on somebody

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.050
that could help resolve the whole problem,

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.910
'cause there's nobody that
could help a homeless person

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.710
better than a homeless person.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.333
And nobody's gonna help the
addict better than an addict.

00:05:47.132 --> 00:05:49.850
I don't know, find some
way, don't give up on us,

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.320
'cause some of us haven't given up,

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.153
and I haven't.

00:05:54.342 --> 00:05:55.792
It's really hard to say that.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.560
If you wanna provide help,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.670
help them with a bus pass,

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.800
but make sure you keep yourself safe.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.767
When you come out here,

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.430
I can't tell you how many
volunteers I see out here

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.650
with sneakers and tennis shoes.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.120
Sorry ma'am, but you're wearing 'em too.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.270
Needles poke through
those shoes real easy.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.870
Be safe.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.340
Don't come out here and
thinking that it's just,

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.330
you know, a walk in the park,

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.440
'cause this is literally

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.855
one of the most dangerous
places you can be.

00:06:24.855 --> 00:06:27.201
(emergency vehicle sirens blaring)

00:06:27.201 --> 00:06:29.780
- That right there, that right there,

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.550
every 20 minutes they are
getting called for an overdose,

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.400
every 20 minutes.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.720
In the year 2017 alone on 17th Street,

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.840
there was 300 overdoses
on 17th Street alone.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.800
That's one street that way.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.760
I counted 39 people last week.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.510
I sat down to myself, "How
many people do I know?"

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.653
It was 39 of my friends
dead in five years.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:54.380
- [Thoraya] I'm sorry about that, man.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.627
- All of us know, we're probably
some of the best at CPR.

00:06:57.627 --> 00:07:00.527
(laughs) Honestly, we know
how to do that (sniffles).

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.580
- Well the reason I
got out here is because

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.770
if you lie, cheat, or
steal things from yourself,

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.620
you're usually doing it to somebody else

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.080
at the same time.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.537
And what goes around comes around.

00:07:15.537 --> 00:07:18.890
(speaking quickly) any time
according to what you've done.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.610
I did stupid things to myself.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:25.160
I've been rich, I've driven
nice cars, nice houses.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.390
But when you get to the point

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:29.640
where you really don't think
you're getting anywhere

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.350
and you're losing connections with people,

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.183
like, with alcohol, or
any substance accordingly.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.580
Mine was alcohol.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.430
And it just drove me to be

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:46.260
self-contained, and it ran my life.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.783
I didn't make any friends,
I don't have any family.

00:07:49.753 --> 00:07:52.020
I lost those when I was a kid.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.270
My dad died when I was five,

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.670
my mom was a heroin
addict, I emancipated her.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.340
I'm one of the ones around here

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.300
that doesn't really need any help.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.330
I got my pension and Social Security.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.420
I was in the Marine Corps for a while,

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.720
and after I got out of that,

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.580
I just kicked around, I
don't wanna be inside.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.200
I don't really wanna
hear anybody's rhetoric

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.410
or about the Bible.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.200
I've read it, I know what it says.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.030
Love others as you want
yourself to be loved.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.380
And if you can live by those rules,

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.320
most likely you're gonna
succeed in whatever you do.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.250
Make sure you keep a hold
of the people around you

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.870
as you grow up and make mistakes.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.130
Those people are the only ones

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.080
that are gonna be forgiving towards you.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:33.440
Anyway, I've been out here
a while, about 12 years,

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.860
and I've helped a lot of
people off the streets

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.920
'cause I have a sound mind
and I am a psychologist,

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.700
went to San Diego State.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.570
But if you get into your own self,

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.350
you think about what you're doing,

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.690
you might be able to help somebody else

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.612
figure out what they
might do for themselves.

00:08:49.612 --> 00:08:50.890
That's about it.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.070
- We're human beings
just like everybody else.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.420
We somebody's mother, brother,

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.630
sister, daughter, child.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.990
We're grandfathers, grandmothers,

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:57.980
we're all of that.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.100
Quit looking down on us

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.450
and thinking that we're always guilty.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.813
You've got some of the best
people in the world homeless.

00:09:02.813 --> 00:09:04.530
I've met some angels.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.350
I've met some people so kind and so sweet

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.780
and so loving

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.160
and they don't have jobs

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.200
and they sleep out here
on the sidewalk with me.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.310
And on the flip side,

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.600
we have the meanest, the
dirtiest, the cruelest.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.020
Institutions tend to
let out the bad people

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:19.030
and throw 'em right where
the homeless population is

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.800
so we have a lot of bad ones

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.380
and we also have a lot of good ones.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.870
This is called The Bottoms.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.300
This is The Bottoms of San Diego.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.160
We are connected to the earth,

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.900
we are the people that's at the bottom.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.780
And when you're at the bottom

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.920
and you see people struggling

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.270
and you see people having a hard time,

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:34.770
the real person, what you see,

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:37.000
without the pretty glamorous, rich, money,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:37.833
all the beautiful things,

00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:39.660
houses, homes, cars, and all that

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.140
then the true feelings come out.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.930
One thing in San Diego,
what needs to be done,

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.130
we need to be able to use the bathroom.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.040
We need a place to wash our clothes.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.920
We need a place to wash our bodies,

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.880
'cause you can't get a
job if you're not clean

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.270
and 'cause you don't have no self-esteem

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.710
to deal with an interviewer

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.980
if you're dirty and smelly and like that.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.770
So that's the main thing.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.020
Help us help ourself.

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.020
And we need to be able
to be on the inside.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.500
Like right now, this year in San Diego,

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.420
it's bitter cold.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.130
A lot of people are dying.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.600
I'm a elder man, I'm 58 years old.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.710
And the weather hurts
people and it kills 'em.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.677
I believe in God, I believe in good,

00:10:13.677 --> 00:10:14.913
and I'm not perfect.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:16.960
None of us are,

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.490
so I try to keep the peace

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.690
and, you know, trying
to keep people inspired

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:24.000
that there is good and there is bad

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.360
but, you know, try to stay more good.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.650
- I'm a native Californian,

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.713
was born out in northern California.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.980
And I think the rent
just got too high for me

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.220
to make it.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.890
You know, I got $1,100 a month.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.853
If your rent's gonna be a thousand,

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.450
you're not gonna do so good with that.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.580
So I think that's basically what it is,

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.160
can't afford the rent as
far as that's concerned.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.190
- I'm just missing love, long story short.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.210
Once I find love again,
I'm back in the wind

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.250
with the money.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.660
But without love then you kinda lost,

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.330
you're kinda confused, you don't know.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.450
But with love, the woman always made sure

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.790
I was taken care of,
food, shelter, driving,

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.530
made me go to work and
give her the whole check,

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.660
but the point is always had a job.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:07.870
I'm missing love.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.890
Minus love is how I got
out here on these streets.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.290
I was never out here.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.380
I can't remember one time I was homeless.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:16.150
People out here with college
degrees, master's, doctorates,

00:11:17.306 --> 00:11:19.226
- [Thoraya] So I guess, can
you give us a follow-up?

00:11:19.226 --> 00:11:20.059
How are you doing?

00:11:20.059 --> 00:11:21.626
- Me and my boyfriend got a place already.

00:11:21.626 --> 00:11:25.546
I'm blessed and I'm
expecting a baby and stuff.

00:11:25.546 --> 00:11:27.516
We're doing good, though.
- That's awesome.

00:11:27.516 --> 00:11:28.349
- And I'm happy.

00:11:28.349 --> 00:11:29.443
We saved a lot of money up

00:11:29.443 --> 00:11:31.566
and we got our own spot by ourself.

00:11:31.566 --> 00:11:33.662
- [Thoraya] I'm so glad
to see you doing well.

00:11:33.662 --> 00:11:34.495
- Thank you.

00:11:34.495 --> 00:11:35.926
I care for the homeless people

00:11:35.926 --> 00:11:37.916
and I try to do my best to help them

00:11:37.916 --> 00:11:39.406
'cause I know how it was.

00:11:39.406 --> 00:11:40.239
- [Thoraya] Is that why

00:11:40.239 --> 00:11:41.206
you're out here today?
- Yeah,

00:11:41.206 --> 00:11:42.996
to talk to them and stuff.

00:11:42.996 --> 00:11:44.226
And they all know me down here.

00:11:44.226 --> 00:11:46.316
I mean, I'm good person.

00:11:46.316 --> 00:11:48.026
- [Thoraya] I know, yeah.

00:11:48.026 --> 00:11:50.902
- I lost my wife two years ago to cancer.

00:11:50.902 --> 00:11:52.473
And

00:11:52.473 --> 00:11:54.523
it was real pretty devastating, you know.

00:11:56.086 --> 00:11:59.226
20 some years together,
you know, my life was good.

00:11:59.226 --> 00:12:02.886
Good working job, and
doing the right thing,

00:12:02.886 --> 00:12:04.616
trying to stay on top of it.

00:12:04.616 --> 00:12:07.159
But it got hard, it got really hard.

00:12:08.116 --> 00:12:10.704
And I got to the point I
couldn't even go home anymore,

00:12:10.704 --> 00:12:12.476
we lived in the same house for 20 years,

00:12:12.476 --> 00:12:14.066
you know how that goes?

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.316
So I had to go.

00:12:15.316 --> 00:12:17.176
And I packed up my stuff one day

00:12:17.176 --> 00:12:21.206
and put all my belongings in storage

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:23.006
and took a leave of absence from my job

00:12:23.006 --> 00:12:24.736
and I walked away from my life.

00:12:25.786 --> 00:12:26.976
- I'm a chronicle homeless

00:12:26.976 --> 00:12:29.199
with physical and mental disabilities.

00:12:29.199 --> 00:12:32.836
I was a caregiver in San Diego Hospice.

00:12:32.836 --> 00:12:35.299
So after that I went sick.

00:12:36.596 --> 00:12:39.209
Unfortunately, I'm not
able to work anymore.

00:12:40.136 --> 00:12:42.996
So I come to this situation.

00:12:42.996 --> 00:12:47.686
As a human being, we fight and request,

00:12:47.686 --> 00:12:50.746
raising the voice to the
authorities to help us out,

00:12:50.746 --> 00:12:52.189
to be out of the streets.

00:12:53.056 --> 00:12:55.366
This unfortunately until right now

00:12:55.366 --> 00:12:57.546
I'm still waiting for that help.

00:12:57.546 --> 00:12:59.026
- [Thoraya] What's the hardest
thing you've been through

00:12:59.026 --> 00:13:00.976
since you've been on the streets?

00:13:00.976 --> 00:13:01.809
- Oh my Lord,

00:13:02.716 --> 00:13:04.376
crimes.

00:13:04.376 --> 00:13:06.576
That's the horrible thing that I ever see.

00:13:06.576 --> 00:13:07.956
I never thought in my life

00:13:07.956 --> 00:13:09.656
to see anything like that.

00:13:09.656 --> 00:13:11.246
I never see any crime like that

00:13:11.246 --> 00:13:13.626
and until right now I'm homeless,

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:15.816
how they kill the people.

00:13:15.816 --> 00:13:19.309
They're stealing in horrible situation.

00:13:20.529 --> 00:13:23.366
How is the city deteriorated?

00:13:23.366 --> 00:13:25.189
And I'm so happy, you know,

00:13:26.466 --> 00:13:29.276
in media about this, you know,

00:13:29.276 --> 00:13:31.726
conversation that we
held between you and me

00:13:31.726 --> 00:13:33.066
and these cameras,

00:13:33.066 --> 00:13:36.246
I hope they can, you know,
a Good Samaritan come

00:13:37.626 --> 00:13:40.266
and give me that hand that I really need-

00:13:40.266 --> 00:13:41.846
- I hope so, too.
- to be outta here.

00:13:41.846 --> 00:13:43.116
Not only for me,

00:13:43.116 --> 00:13:44.033
for the rest of the peoples,

00:13:44.033 --> 00:13:45.566
the human being that we are.

00:13:45.566 --> 00:13:47.786
We proud to be an Americans.

00:13:47.786 --> 00:13:49.106
That's what really we need,

00:13:49.106 --> 00:13:50.609
and I'm proud to be who I am.

00:13:53.119 --> 00:13:53.956
- Hey everyone.

00:13:53.956 --> 00:13:55.146
I mentioned in part one of this

00:13:55.146 --> 00:13:56.636
how hard it was to decide

00:13:56.636 --> 00:13:58.836
to film and upload the episode.

00:13:58.836 --> 00:14:01.859
And it was just as hard
if not harder this time.

00:14:02.956 --> 00:14:04.326
I tend to overthink things

00:14:04.326 --> 00:14:06.196
when it comes to touchy subjects

00:14:06.196 --> 00:14:08.176
and vulnerable spaces like this one.

00:14:08.176 --> 00:14:10.846
I just really think that there
are a lot of misconceptions

00:14:10.846 --> 00:14:12.836
when it comes to the homeless community.

00:14:12.836 --> 00:14:15.326
And I also believe that the best way

00:14:15.326 --> 00:14:16.956
to solve problems like this

00:14:16.956 --> 00:14:20.286
is to ask hard questions
and share real stories.

00:14:20.286 --> 00:14:21.896
So I hope you learned a lot

00:14:21.896 --> 00:14:24.656
by hearing these stories
because I know I did.

00:14:24.656 --> 00:14:25.816
I'm gonna do everything I can

00:14:25.816 --> 00:14:28.326
to give back to my
community here in San Diego.

00:14:28.326 --> 00:14:31.246
And again, I hope you'll
do the same with yours.

00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:32.079
That's pretty much it.

00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:34.026
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:14:34.026 --> 00:14:37.726
Be kind, stay safe, and
I'll see you next week.

00:14:37.726 --> 00:14:40.809
(gentle piano music)

